      "name": "overview",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "html",
          "name": "survey_overview",
          "html": "<h3>Purpose</h3><p>This survey asks Wyoming voters how primary elections should work. The goal is to measure public opinion on voter participation, party nomination rights, privacy, election administration, deadline timing, benefits, concerns, and public reporting.</p><h3>How responses will be used</h3><p>This survey is a tool to gather and report registered Wyoming voter survey results in aggregate. Exact question wording, response options, collection dates, sample size, verification method, and revision notes will be published with the results. Individual responses will remain confidential.</p><h3>Verification note</h3><p>For Wyoming voters, responses may be checked against a voter-file data set obtained from the Wyoming Secretary of State. The current verification file reflects registered voter records as of August 2025.</p><p>This serves two purposes:</p><ul><li>It helps report survey results from verified registered Wyoming voters.</li><li>It can help a respondent see whether submitted information matches a registered voter record in the August 2025 file.</li></ul><p>A match confirms the respondent appeared in that data file. It does not confirm later registration changes, current party affiliation, or current voter status after August 2025. If a respondent registered, moved, or updated voter information after August 2025, the match result may need additional review.</p><p>Where possible, county, State House district, and State Senate district will come from the voter-file match instead of asking extra questions. Verified and unverified results should be reported separately.</p><h3>Background note</h3><p>Wyoming currently uses an affiliation-based system for major party primary ballots. Registered voters must declare or change party affiliation before receiving a major party primary ballot. In 2026, the party-affiliation change deadline was May 13, and candidate filing opened May 14.</p><p>Wyoming's Constitution also says elections shall be &ldquo;open, free and equal&rdquo; and protects the &ldquo;untrammeled exercise&rdquo; of suffrage. This survey asks how voters believe that principle should be balanced with party nomination rights, election administration, and voter privacy.</p><h3>Terms used in this survey</h3><p><strong>Affiliation-based primary:</strong> A primary system where a voter's party affiliation determines which party ballot the voter may receive.</p><p><strong>Ballot-choice primary:</strong> A primary system where a voter chooses one available party ballot when voting, and that ballot choice does not automatically change voter registration.</p><p><strong>Open-to-unaffiliated model:</strong> A primary system where unaffiliated voters may choose one party ballot, while voters already affiliated with a party follow affiliation rules.</p><h3>References used to draft this survey</h3><p>These links are provided for voters who want to review the source material. Reading them is optional and is not required to answer the survey. The questions below are intended to measure opinion, not persuade.</p><ul><li>Wyoming Constitution, Article 1</li><li>Wyoming Election Code, W.S. 22-5-212</li><li>Wyoming Election Code, W.S. 22-5-214</li><li>Wyoming Secretary of State, 2026 Key Election Dates</li><li>NCSL, State Primary Election Types</li><li>U.S. Supreme Court cases on party association and primary participation</li></ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "survey_questions",
      "title": "Survey Questions",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "familiarity_with_current_rules",
          "title": "1. How familiar are you with Wyoming's current primary election rules?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Very familiar",
            "Somewhat familiar",
            "Slightly familiar",
            "Unfamiliar",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "preferred_primary_system",
          "title": "2. Which primary system do you prefer for Wyoming?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Keep the current closed primary system",
            "Allow unaffiliated voters to choose one party primary ballot",
            "Allow any registered voter to choose one party primary ballot",
            "Let each major party decide who may participate",
            "Use one ballot with all candidates, with the top two advancing",
            "Not sure"
          ],
          "showOtherItem": true,
          "otherText": "Other"
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "who_should_vote_in_major_party_primary",
          "title": "3. Who should be able to vote in a major party primary?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Only voters registered with that party",
            "Voters registered with that party, plus unaffiliated voters",
            "Any registered voter, choosing only one party ballot",
            "Each major party should decide",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "affiliation_deadline_timing",
          "title": "4. When should the party-affiliation deadline be set?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Before candidate filing opens",
            "After candidate filing closes",
            "On primary election day",
            "A deadline is unnecessary if voters choose one party ballot when voting",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "which_matters_more",
          "title": "5. Which matters more to you in a primary election system?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Party members choosing party nominees",
            "More registered voters having access to meaningful primary choices",
            "A balanced approach between both",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "preferred_voter_privacy_approach",
          "title": "6. Which voter privacy approach do you prefer?",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Party registration should determine which primary ballot a voter receives",
            "Voters should choose one available party ballot when voting",
            "Either approach is acceptable",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "strongest_reason_closed_primary",
          "title": "7. What is the strongest reason to keep a closed primary? Pick one.",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Party members should choose party nominees",
            "Closed primaries may reduce strategic crossover voting",
            "Party identity and party accountability may be clearer",
            "Election rules may be easier to administer",
            "I do not see a strong reason",
            "Not sure"
          ],
          "showOtherItem": true,
          "otherText": "Other"
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "strongest_reason_more_open_primary",
          "title": "8. What is the strongest reason to support a more open primary? Pick one.",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "More registered voters can participate",
            "Unaffiliated voters have more meaningful ballot access",
            "Voters have more privacy in ballot choice",
            "Candidates may speak to a broader voter base",
            "I do not see a strong reason",
            "Not sure"
          ],
          "showOtherItem": true,
          "otherText": "Other"
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "biggest_concern_current_closed_system",
          "title": "9. What is your biggest concern about Wyoming's current closed primary system? Pick one.",
          "isRequired": true,
          "choices": [
            "Some registered voters have fewer meaningful primary choices",
            "Party-affiliation deadlines happen before voters know the full candidate list",
            "Voters may change affiliation mainly to access a useful ballot",
            "Unaffiliated voters have limited participation",
            "I do not have a major concern",
            "Not sure"
